<h3>Carrier Category and Fuel Variables</h3>
<p>The type of trailer or vehicle category selected also impacts pricing. Standard open trucks are generally more affordable, while enclosed, air-conditioned cargo containers command a premium for enhanced security and protection against weather.</p>
<p>Additionally, fuel surcharges are dynamic variables that adjust based on real-time diesel prices. These surcharges are typically calculated as a percentage of the base fare, ensuring that carriers can manage fluctuating energy costs without altering their core service rates.</p>
